  <p>PluriFin grants the User a <strong>non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable on breach</strong> license, for personal use of the App.</p>
  <p>The User may NOT:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Decompile, disassemble or reverse-engineer the software (except as allowed by Italian Law 633/1941 art. 64-quater)</li>
    <li>Remove, alter or hide notices, copyright, trademarks</li>
    <li>Resell, sublicense, rent or distribute the App</li>
    <li>Use the App for unlawful, fraudulent or third-party-harming purposes</li>
    <li>Bypass technical protection measures (e.g. subscription validation)</li>
    <li>Use the App to provide professional services to third parties</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The User MAY:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the App for personal and family finances</li>
    <li>Export their data and migrate to other apps</li>
    <li>Keep local copies</li>
    <li>Uninstall at any time</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 id="s6">6. Account and security</h2>
  <p>The App <strong>requires no PluriFin account</strong>. Everything is local to the device. The Google Play account associated with subscription purchase is fully managed by Google.</p>
  <p>The User is responsible for device security: lock screen, backup, loss. PluriFin cannot recover portfolio data if the device is lost without prior manual export.</p>
  <h2 id="s7">7. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <h3 id="s7-1">7.1 General</h3>
  <p>The App is provided "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE", without warranties of any kind except those non-excludable by applicable law (in particular Italian Legislative Decree 206/2005 -- Consumer Code for EU consumers).</p>
  <h3 id="s7-2">7.2 Express exclusions</h3>
  <p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, PluriFin is NOT liable for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Investment decisions made by the User based on data or analyses shown by the App</li>
    <li>Financial losses of any size, including loss of capital, lost profit, lost opportunity</li>
    <li>Errors, delays, unavailability or inaccuracy of market data provided by third parties (EODHD, FMP and the other providers of Privacy Policy section 3.5)</li>
    <li>Errors, hallucinations, outdated or misleading content in AI model responses (Gemini)</li>
    <li>Parsing errors of broker CSV/PDF statements (formats change without notice)</li>
    <li>Unavailability or errors of Google Play in reporting to the App the status of a purchase or a subscription</li>
    <li>Local data loss due to uninstall, device malfunction, missing User backup</li>
    <li>Compromise of the User's device (root, jailbreak, malware)</li>
  </ul>
  <h3 id="s7-3">7.3 Quantitative cap</h3>
  <p>In any case, save for legal exclusions for wilful misconduct or gross negligence (Italian Civil Code art. 1229), PluriFin's total liability to the User, for any cause, is capped at the higher of:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>EUR 50.00</strong> (fifty euros)</li>
    <li>The amount actually paid by the User for Premium in the 12 months before the event</li>
  </ul>
  <h3 id="s7-4">7.4 Non-waivable consumer rights</h3>
  <p>Nothing in these Terms limits or excludes the User-consumer's rights under Italian Consumer Code (D.Lgs. 206/2005), particularly:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Legal warranty of conformity (arts. 128-135-vicies)</li>
    <li>Right of withdrawal where applicable (arts. 49+, with the exclusion for digital content under art. 59.1.o where the User explicitly agreed to immediate execution)</li>
    <li>Protection against unfair clauses (arts. 33-37)</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 id="s8">8. Third-party services and content</h2>
  <p>The App optionally integrates with third-party services. The User accepts that:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>AI analyses are provided by Google Gemini, subject to <a href="https://ai.google.dev/terms">Google Gemini API Terms</a></li>
    <li>Real-time market data is provided by EODHD and/or FMP, subject to their respective terms</li>
    <li>Payment goes through Google Play, subject to <a href="https://play.google.com/about/play-terms/">Google Play Policies</a></li>
    <li>Hosting of legal docs and web app is on GitHub Pages, subject to <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/github-terms/github-terms-of-service">GitHub Terms</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>PluriFin does not control these services and is not responsible for malfunctions, modifications, suspensions or terminations decided by them.</p>
  <h2 id="s9">9. Changes to the Terms</h2>
  <p>PluriFin can change these Terms. Material changes will be notified in app, via re-consent screen on the first launch after the update.</p>
  <p>If the User does not accept the changes they may uninstall the App and request a refund of the unused subscription via Google Play, per Play policy.</p>
  <h2 id="s10">10. Termination</h2>
  <h3 id="s10-1">10.1 By the User</h3>
  <p>The User can terminate at any time by:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Disabling subscription renewal in Google Play</li>
    <li>Uninstalling the App</li>
  </ol>
  <p>No penalties or formalities required.</p>
  <h3 id="s10-2">10.2 By PluriFin</h3>
  <p>PluriFin can terminate and revoke the license for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Material breach of these Terms by the User</li>
    <li>Fraudulent use</li>
    <li>Attempts to circumvent anti-tamper / anti-piracy protections</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Where termination is the User's fault, no proportional refund is provided.</p>
  <h3 id="s10-3">10.3 Service shutdown by PluriFin</h3>
  <p>PluriFin reserves the right to discontinue development or availability of the App with at least <strong>90 days notice</strong> via:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>In app</li>
    <li>Marketing site</li>
    <li>Email to Premium subscribers</li>
  </ul>
  <p>In case of shutdown, paid subscriptions are honored to natural expiry, or refunded pro-rata via Google Play.</p>
