  <p>The User acquires no rights over PluriFin trademarks, logos or code.</p>
  <h2 id="s12">12. Personal data protection</h2>
  <p>Processing of the User's personal data is governed by the <strong>Privacy Policy</strong> (<code>legal/privacy_policy.md</code>), integral part of these Terms.</p>
  <h2 id="s13">13. Financial disclaimer</h2>
  <p>The <strong>Financial Disclaimer</strong> (<code>legal/disclaimer_financial.md</code>) is integral part of these Terms and must be read and accepted before using the App.</p>
  <h2 id="s14">14. Jurisdiction and applicable law</h2>
  <p>These Terms are governed by <strong>Italian law</strong>.</p>
  <p>For disputes with consumer Users, the competent forum is the User's residence or elective domicile per art. 66-bis of Italian Consumer Code (D.Lgs. 206/2005), unless a different choice is allowed by law.</p>
  <p>For non-consumer Users (professional use), the exclusive forum is <strong>Milan (Italy)</strong>, per arts. 18 and 20 of the Italian Code of Civil Procedure as the forum of the controller domiciled in Italy.</p>
  <p>In case of discrepancy between the language versions of this document, the Italian text prevails.</p>
  <h2 id="s15">15. Alternative dispute resolution (ADR)</h2>
  <p>The consumer User may use the EU Commission ODR platform: <a href="https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/">https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/</a></p>
  <h2 id="s16">16. Severability</h2>
  <p>If any clause is declared invalid or ineffective by a competent authority, remaining clauses stay in force.</p>
  <h2 id="s17">17. Communications</h2>
  <p>PluriFin's communications to the User happen via:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>In app (consent screens)</li>
    <li>Email if the User has provided one</li>
    <li>Marketing site</li>
  </ul>
  <p>User communications to PluriFin via email to the appropriate address (see section 12 of the Privacy Policy).</p>
